# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's M1 package (matmul grids for the 13x10 compute grid; docs/tp4-fusion-m1.md): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the fusion integration branch (with fusion-wp/M1.json placed by make_fusion_profiles.py --write and fusion-wp/M1-tp-addresses.patch applied) and
# push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its
# author. M1/ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag the pack's B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# M1P2 (TIMED, M1): the LEVER (B1) of the SOLO prefill ladder ABAB: c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-grid13, UNPROFILED, with C2_TELEMETRY=1. prefill_ladder_solo: four real-code prompts of about 4,096 / 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens, ONE request at a time
# with nothing else running, a 16-token answer: the time to first token and the prefill rate of each rung. The LEVER arm adds only QWEN_FAST_GRID13=1 to the combined fusion arm.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean (the lever arm has its engaged lines and no fell-back line), the `[TELEMETRY]` lines (`decode check ok`; the loaded AICLK median and any throttler, per chip, over each rung); then
# python3 scripts/ci/prefill_ladder_report.py <control results> --second <lever results> for the pairs (M1P1, M1P2) and (M1P3, M1P4): the per-rung TTFT and prefill rate, the lever over the control, and the
# control-to-control spread (M1P1 against M1P3) that a gain has to beat. The text of every answer must equal the control's (the greedy answer cannot depend on the prefill grid). ESTIMATE to beat (not a measurement):
# the three fused all-gather matmuls are 85.7 of the 266 ms of non-SDPA kernel time of a 2,048-row chunk; if the busiest core's output rows fall from 8 to 6 (12 columns, M block 6) and the block
# efficiency holds that is -25 percent of them (21 ms a chunk), at 70 percent of that efficiency 14 ms; the range is 6 to 20 ms a chunk (central 14), i.e. 0.4 to 1.5 s (central 1.0 s) of the 36.8 s TTFT at
# 131,072 tokens and about 2 s of the ~98 s at 253,920. Duration (estimate): 25 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-grid13
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=solo prefill ladder: the protocol fixes its test list, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
C2_TELEMETRY=1
